 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "hero-01",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Fixed verbs. Past and order.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-02",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Two kinds of verb that never change.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-03",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A past verb and an order verb are always fixed.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-04",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Their ending tells you who did the action.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "hero-05",
   "scene": "hero",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And that ending never moves for iʿrāb.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-01",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter one. Which verbs are fixed?",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-02",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Arabic has three kinds of verb.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-03",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Two of them are fixed in every form.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-title-04",
   "scene": "c01-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَبْنِيٌّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-01",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The first is the past verb. An action that is done.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "item:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-02",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَ",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-03",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "He wrote. It is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-04",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The second is the order verb. You tell someone to act.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "item:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-05",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "اُكْتُبْ",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-06",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Write! It is fixed too.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-07",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The third is the present verb. It is mostly flexible. Its ending changes.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "item:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-cols-08",
   "scene": "c01-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "We study it in Stage 8.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-01",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In this unit we only use past and order verbs.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c01-tip-02",
   "scene": "c01-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Leave the present verb for later.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-01",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter two. The past verb. Fourteen persons.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-02",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Learn this table by heart.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-title-03",
   "scene": "c02-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Each pronoun from unit one has its own past form.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-01",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Start with he, they two, and they. These are for men.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-02",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-03",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَا",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-04",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبُوا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "row:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-05",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Now she, they two, and they, for women.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-06",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَتْ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-07",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَتَا",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-08",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْنَ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "row:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-09",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Now you. One man, two men, and many men.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-10",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتَ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-11",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُمَا",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-12",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُمْ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "row:8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-13",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "You again. One woman, two women, and many women.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-14",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتِ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-15",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُمَا",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:10"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-16",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُنَّ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "row:11"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-17",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Last, I and we.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-18",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "row:12"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-19",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْنَا",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "row:13"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-table-20",
   "scene": "c02-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "That is the whole table.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "unhl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-01",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "There are fourteen persons, but only thirteen written forms.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-02",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُمَا",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": [
    "hl:is used for two men and for two women"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-tip-03",
   "scene": "c02-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "You two wrote. It is used for two men and for two women.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-01",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Three examples.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-02",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "I went to the mosque.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-03",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَنَا ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى المَسْجِدِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "read:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-04",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The verb has the ending for I.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-05",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "She sat in the room.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-06",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "هِيَ جَلَسَتْ فِي الغُرْفَةِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "read:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-07",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The verb has the form for she.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-08",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "We did not go out of the house.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-09",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "نَحْنُ مَا خَرَجْنَا مِنَ البَيْتِ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "read:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-10",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Look at the small word before the verb.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "note:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-11",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "مَا",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": [
    "hl:مَا"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c02-examples-12",
   "scene": "c02-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Before a past verb, it means did not. We come back to it in chapter five.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-01",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter three. The ending is the doer.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-02",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Most endings of the past verb are attached pronouns.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-03",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The pronoun is the doer. It is fixed, in the place of rafʿ.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-title-04",
   "scene": "c03-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي مَحَلِّ رَفْعٍ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-01",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here are the doer endings.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-02",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This ending means I.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-03",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "You, for one man.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-04",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "You, for one woman.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-05",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And we.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-06",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "You all, for men.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-07",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They, for men.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-08",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "They, for women.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-09",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And they two.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "item:7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-words-10",
   "scene": "c03-words",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Each of these endings is the doer.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-01",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "But one ending is different.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-02",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَتْ",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-03",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "She wrote. Here the ending only shows that the doer is feminine.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "hl:only shows that the doer is feminine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-04",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is a ḥarf, with no place.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "hl:It is a ḥarf, with no place"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-05",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The doer is hidden. It is she.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:The doer is hidden"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-rule-06",
   "scene": "c03-rule",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "هِيَ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-01",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "So compare three forms.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-02",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "First, a hidden doer.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-03",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَ",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-04",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "There is no ending. The doer is hidden. It is he.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-05",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Second, a hidden doer again.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-06",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَتْ",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-07",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This ending is a ḥarf. The doer is hidden. It is she.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-08",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Third, an attached doer.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "item:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-09",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبْتُ",
   "pause": 0.45,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-cols-10",
   "scene": "c03-cols",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The ending is the doer, in the place of rafʿ.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tip-01",
   "scene": "c03-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "When a noun is the doer, the verb has no doer ending.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tip-02",
   "scene": "c03-tip",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c03-tip-03",
   "scene": "c03-tip",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The student wrote. The student is the doer.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-01",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Chapter four. What the past verb is built on.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-02",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "A fixed word is built on one fixed mark. A past verb is built on fatha, damma or sukūn.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "sub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-03",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Look at the last letter of the verb itself, before any doer pronoun.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-table-01",
   "scene": "c04-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The past verb is built on fatha when it has no ending.",
   "pause": 0.25,
   "cues": [
    "row:0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-table-02",
   "scene": "c04-table",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is also built on fatha before the ḥarf for she, and before the alif for they two.",
